FIX FE RACE-TYPE DIALOG (817): reconstruct + int-type nested-table handlers @0x46a724

Confirming a race MODE in the dialog fixed by patch 816 enters a THIRD-level nested table
@0x46a724 (race-TYPE sub-dialog: Championship / Practice / Time Trials / Multiplayer,
dispatched by FUN_00452f80). Same two defects as patch 816: records 2/3 SETUP handlers were
unexported raw VAs (0x4531a4 "Time Trials", 0x4531c4 "Multiplayer") -> reconstructed 1:1 from
asm (label slots 0x46a6f0/0x46a704 + Setup_Screen_Text, mirror of FUN_00453164); and all four
setups were void(void) while the nested dispatch types them `code`=int() -> widened to
int(void) (value discarded). The four ACTION handlers (Select_Champ/Pract/TimeT/Multi) already
return i32 and are registered. New string macros for 0x46efb4/0x46efc8; new VAs registered in
dd2_dispatch.c. Completes the race mode->type configuration flow reached from the race-options
button (main screen 0).

